// Headless components: each is one kind of control as a part of the window's tree, made
// once, that is all the control is to the hand, the keyboard and a screen reader, and draws nothing.
// Its look is its caller's: an app's library of looks is written over these, and writes looks only.
//
// Three layers:
//   1. Framework (packages/view): tree, layout, motion, focus, keymap, a11y, virtual lists.
//   2. Headless components (packages/headless): pointer, keyboard, and screen-reader behavior per control kind.
//   3. Look libraries: visual styling and presentation over headless components.
